DOTFILES(7)                 Nix Configuration Manual                DOTFILES(7)

NAME
       dotfiles - Nix-based system and user configuration for macOS, NixOS,
                  and non-NixOS Linux

SYNOPSIS
       Darwin (macOS):
           darwin-rebuild switch --flake .#mbp

       NixOS:
           nixos-rebuild switch --flake .#remote-dev

       Standalone Home Manager (non-NixOS Linux):
           home-manager switch --flake .#whexy@linux
           home-manager switch --flake .#whexy@linux-aarch64

DESCRIPTION
       This repository contains declarative system configurations using Nix
       flakes. It supports three deployment targets:

       1. macOS systems via nix-darwin
       2. NixOS systems via nixosConfigurations
       3. Non-NixOS Linux via standalone home-manager

       The configuration provides a consistent development environment across
       all platforms, including shell configuration, development tools, and
       editor setup.

TARGETS
   darwinConfigurations.mbp
       Target:     macOS (aarch64-darwin)
       Type:       nix-darwin system configuration
       Profile:    Personal workstation with full GUI support

       Includes:
           - System-wide package management
           - Home Manager integration for user environment
           - macOS-specific settings (Aerospace window manager)
           - Development tools and LSP servers
           - Ghostty terminal configuration

       Deploy:
           darwin-rebuild switch --flake /path/to/dotfiles#mbp

   nixosConfigurations.remote-dev
       Target:     NixOS (x86_64-linux)
       Type:       Full NixOS system configuration
       Profile:    Remote development server

       Includes:
           - Complete NixOS system management
           - Boot loader configuration (systemd-boot)
           - Network management and SSH server
           - Docker and Tailscale services
           - Development environment with Home Manager

       Deploy:
           nixos-rebuild switch --flake /path/to/dotfiles#remote-dev

   homeConfigurations."whexy@linux"
       Target:     Non-NixOS Linux (x86_64-linux)
       Type:       Standalone home-manager configuration
       Profile:    Development environment for existing Linux systems

       Includes:
           - User-level package management via home.packages
           - Shell configuration (zsh, fzf, starship, zoxide)
           - Terminal multiplexer (tmux with catppuccin theme)
           - Git with SSH signing and 1Password integration
           - Neovim with custom Lua configuration
           - Development tools (compilers, LSPs, formatters)

       Deploy:
           home-manager switch --flake /path/to/dotfiles#whexy@linux

       Prerequisites:
           - Nix package manager installed
           - Home Manager available (via nix profile or channels)

   homeConfigurations."whexy@linux-aarch64"
       Target:     Non-NixOS Linux (aarch64-linux)
       Type:       Standalone home-manager configuration
       Profile:    Same as whexy@linux for ARM64 systems

       Deploy:
           home-manager switch --flake /path/to/dotfiles#whexy@linux-aarch64

ARCHITECTURE
       Home-manager modules are written as standalone configs first, then
       wrapped for NixOS/Darwin via home/wrapper.nix.

       .
       |-- flake.nix              Main entry point
       |-- home/                  Pure home-manager modules (standalone-first)
       |   |-- base.nix           Shell, tmux, vim + base packages
       |   |-- dev.nix            Imports base + dev tools, LSPs
       |   |-- personal.nix       Imports dev + GUI apps
       |   |-- standalone.nix     Entry point for non-NixOS Linux
       |   |-- wrapper.nix        Adapts modules for NixOS/Darwin
       |   |-- packages.nix       Shared package definitions
       |   |-- base/              Base sub-modules
       |   |-- dev/               Dev sub-modules
       |   |-- macos/             macOS-specific home modules
       |   `-- personal/          Personal home modules
       |-- system/                NixOS/Darwin system modules
       |   |-- base.nix           Nix settings, overlays
       |   |-- dev.nix            Wraps home/dev.nix
       |   |-- personal.nix       Wraps home/personal.nix + fonts
       |   |-- macos.nix          macOS system settings
       |   `-- user.nix           User account settings
       |-- hosts/                 Host-specific configurations
       |   |-- mbp/               MacBook Pro (Darwin)
       |   `-- remote-dev/        Development server (NixOS)
       |-- overlays/              Nix overlays
       |   `-- mk-op-wrapped.nix  1Password wrapper for secrets
       `-- nvim/                  Neovim configuration (Lua)

FILES
       home/base.nix
           Base home-manager config. Imports base/shell.nix, base/tmux.nix,
           base/vim.nix. Adds packages.base to home.packages.

       home/dev.nix
           Development home-manager config. Imports base.nix + dev/*.nix.
           Adds packages.dev to home.packages, enables gpg-agent.

       home/standalone.nix
           Entry point for non-NixOS Linux. Imports dev.nix and sets
           home.username and home.homeDirectory defaults.

       home/wrapper.nix
           Adapter that wraps a home-manager module in home-manager.users.whexy
           for use in NixOS/Darwin system configurations.

       home/packages.nix
           Single source of truth for package lists. Exports packages.base
           and packages.dev attribute sets.

       system/base.nix
           Base system config. Nix settings, flakes, unfree packages.

       system/dev.nix
           Development system config. Imports home/dev.nix via wrapper.

       system/personal.nix
           Personal system config. Imports home/personal.nix + fonts.

EXAMPLES
       Initial setup on a new non-NixOS Linux machine:

           # Install Nix (if not already installed)
           sh <(curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install) --daemon

           # Enable flakes
           mkdir -p ~/.config/nix
           echo "experimental-features = nix-command flakes" >> ~/.config/nix/nix.conf

           # Deploy configuration
           nix run home-manager/release-25.11 -- switch \
               --flake github:whexy/dotfiles#whexy@linux

       Update configuration after changes:

           home-manager switch --flake .#whexy@linux

       Build without switching (dry run):

           home-manager build --flake .#whexy@linux

ENVIRONMENT
       The configuration expects the following for full functionality:

       1Password CLI
           Required for secrets injection (API keys, tokens).
           The mkOpWrapped overlay wraps commands to fetch secrets at runtime.

       SSH Agent (1Password)
           SSH configuration expects 1Password SSH agent at:
               ~/.1password/agent.sock (Linux)
               ~/Library/Group Containers/2BUA8C4S2C.com.1password/t/agent.sock (macOS)

CUSTOMIZATION
       To use this configuration for a different user:

       1. Fork the repository

       2. Update homeConfigurations in flake.nix with your username

       3. Modify user-specific settings in:
           - home/dev/git.nix (user.name, user.email, signing keys)
           - home/dev/ssh.nix (host configurations)

       4. Update system/user.nix for Darwin systems

